(I need not point out to your Committee the necessity of differentiating) Tj T*
(between the Stock Exchange as such and those who use the Stock) Tj T*
(Exchange.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Most of the complaints against the Stock Exchange arise from the action) Tj T*
(of those outside of its organization and over whose conduct it has no) Tj T*
(control. No doubt there have at times been shortcomings and laxity of) Tj T*
(methods in the administration of the Stock Exchange just as there have) Tj T*
(been in every other institution administered by human hands and brains.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: _Should the Exchange be regulated?_]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Some things were, if not approved, at least tolerated in the past which) Tj T*
(are not in accord with the ethical conception of to-day.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The same thing can be said of almost every other institution, even of) Tj T*
(Congress. Until a few years ago, the acceptance of campaign) Tj T*
(contributions from corporations, the acceptance of railroad passes by) Tj T*
(Congressmen and Senators were regular practices which did not shock the) Tj T*
(conscience either of the recipients or of the public. Now they have) Tj T*
(rightly been made and are looked upon as crimes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Ethical conceptions change; the limits of what is morally permissible) Tj T*
(are drawn tighter. That is the normal process by which civilization) Tj T*
(moves forward.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Stock Exchange has never sought to resist the coming of that higher) Tj T*
(standard. On the contrary, in its own sphere it has ever endeavored to) Tj T*
(maintain an exemplary standard, and it has ever shown itself ready and) Tj T*
(willing to introduce better methods whenever experience showed them to) Tj T*
(be wise or suggestion showed them to be called for.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: _Should the Exchange be regulated?_]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In its regulations for the admission of securities to quotation, in the) Tj T*
(publicity of its dealings, in the solvency of its members, in its rules) Tj T*
(regulating their conduct and the enforcement of such rules, the New) Tj T*
(York Stock Exchange is at least on a par with any other Stock Exchange) Tj T*
(in the world, and, in fact, more advanced than almost any other.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The outside market on the curb could not exist if it were not for the) Tj T*
(stringency of the requirements in the interest of the public which the) Tj T*
(Stock Exchange imposes in respect of the admission of securities to) Tj T*
(trading within its walls and jurisdiction.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There is no other Stock Exchange in existence in which the public has) Tj T*
(that control over the execution of orders, which is given to it by the) Tj T*
(practice--unique to the New York Stock Exchange--of having every single) Tj T*
(transaction immediately recorded when made and publicly announced on) Tj T*
(the ticker and on the daily transaction sheet.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I am familiar with the Stock Exchanges of London, Berlin and Paris, and) Tj T*
