(effects.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: _Short selling Is it justifiable?_]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I am informed on good authority--though I cannot personally vouch for) Tj T*
(the correctness of the information--that there is no short selling on) Tj T*
(one nowadays fairly important Stock Exchange,--that of Tokyo, Japan.) Tj T*
(You will have seen in the papers that when President Wilson's peace) Tj T*
(message \(or was it the German Chancellor's peace speech?\) became known) Tj T*
(in Tokyo, the Stock Exchange there was thrown into a panic of such) Tj T*
(violence that it had to close its doors. It attempted to reopen a) Tj T*
(couple of days later, but after a short while of trading was again) Tj T*
(compelled to suspend.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Assuming my information to be correct, you have here an illuminating) Tj T*
(instance of cause and effect.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Short selling does become a wrong when and to the extent that the) Tj T*
(methods and intent of the short seller are wrong.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The short seller who goes about like a raging lion [or bear] seeking) Tj T*
(whom he may devour; he who deliberately smashes values by dint of) Tj T*
(manipulation or artificially intensified selling amounting in effect to) Tj T*
(manipulation, or by spreading alarm through untrue reports or even) Tj T*
(through merely unverified rumors, does wrong and ought to be punished.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: _Short selling Is it justifiable?_]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Perhaps the Stock Exchange authorities are not always alert enough and) Tj T*
(thorough enough in running down and punishing deliberate wreckers of) Tj T*
(values and spreaders of evil omen; perhaps there is altogether not) Tj T*
(enough energy and determination in dealing with the grave and dangerous) Tj T*
(evil of rumor mongering on the Stock Exchange and in brokers' offices.) Tj T*
(But after all even Congress, with the machinery of almost unlimited) Tj T*
(power at its hand, does not always seem to find it quite easy to hunt) Tj T*
(the wicked rumor-mongers to their lairs and subject them to adequate) Tj T*
(punishment.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Yet the unwarranted assailing of a man's good name is a more grievous) Tj T*
(and heinous offence than the assailing, by dint even of false reports,) Tj T*
(of the market prices of his possessions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
