() Tj T*
(Such a law would be analogous in its purpose and function to the Pure) Tj T*
(Food Law, Any, let us call it, "anti-fleecing" law which went beyond) Tj T*
(that purpose and function would overshoot the mark. The Pure Food Law) Tj T*
(does not pretend to prescribe how much a man should eat, when he should) Tj T*
(eat or what is good or bad for him to eat, but it does prescribe that) Tj T*
(the ingredients of what is sold to him as food must be honestly and) Tj T*
(publicly stated. The same principle should prevail in respect of the) Tj T*
(offering and sale of securities.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If a drug contains water, the quantity or proportion must be shown on) Tj T*
(the label, so that a man cannot sell you a bottle filled with water) Tj T*
(when you think you are buying a tonic. In the same way the proportion) Tj T*
(of water in a stock issue should be plainly and publicly shown.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The purchaser should not be permitted to be under the impression that) Tj T*
(he is buying a share in tangible assets when, as a matter of fact, he) Tj T*
(is buying expectations, earning capacity or goodwill. These may be, and) Tj T*
(often are, very valuable elements, but the purchaser ought to be) Tj T*
(enabled to judge as to that with the facts plainly and clearly before) Tj T*
(him.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: _Does the public get fleeced?_]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The main evil of watered stock lies not in the presence of water, but) Tj T*
(in the concealment or coloring of that liquid. Notwithstanding the) Tj T*
(unenviable reputation which the popular view attaches to watered stock,) Tj T*
(there are distinctly two sides to that question, always provided that) Tj T*
(the strictest and fullest publicity is given to all pertinent facts) Tj T*
(concerning the creation and nature of the stock.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
