() Tj T*
(The fluctuations of the stock market represent the views, the judgment) Tj T*
(and the conditions of thousands of people all over the country, and) Tj T*
(indeed, in normal times, all over the world.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The current which sends market prices up or down is far stronger than) Tj T*
(any man or combination of men. It would sweep any man or men aside like) Tj T*
(driftwood if they stood in its way or attempted to deflect it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: _Do "big men" put the market up or down?_]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(True, men at times discern the approach of that current from afar off) Tj T*
(and back their judgment singly, or sometimes even a few of them) Tj T*
(together, as to its time and effect. They may hasten a little the) Tj T*
(advent of that current, they may a little intensify its effect, but) Tj T*
(they have not the power to either unloosen it or stop it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If by the term "big men" you mean Bankers, let me add that a genuine) Tj T*
(Banker has very little time and, generally speaking, equally little) Tj T*
(inclination to speculate, and that his very training and occupation) Tj T*
(unfit him to be a successful speculator.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Banker's training is to judge intrinsic values, his outlook must be) Tj T*
(broad and comprehensive, his plans must take account of the longer) Tj T*
(future. The Speculator's business is to discern and take advantage of) Tj T*
(immediate situations, his outlook is for tomorrow, or anyhow for the) Tj T*
(early future; he must indeed be able at times to disregard intrinsic) Tj T*
(values.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Sidenote: _Do "big men" put the market up or down?_]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The temperamental and mental qualifications of the Banker and) Tj T*
(Speculator are fundamentally conflicting and it hardly ever happens) Tj T*
(that these qualifications are successfully combined in one and the same) Tj T*
(person. The Banker as a stock market factor is vastly and strangely) Tj T*
(over-estimated, even by the Stock Exchange fraternity itself.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(May I add, in parenthesis, that a sharp line of demarcation exists) Tj T*
(between the speculator and the gambler? The former has a useful and) Tj T*
